### Scenario 30 — Happy path: claim → intake → assessment → tenant response → penalty applied
### IntelliJ HTTP Client syntax (`> {% client.global.set(...) %}` captures ids).
### Prereq: run 00-smoke.http section 0 first (or have landlord/tenant/admin seeded).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@adminEmail = admin@blps.local
@adminPass = adminpass
@landlordEmail = landlord@blps.local
@landlordPass = landpass
@tenantEmail = tenant@blps.local
@tenantPass = tenantpass

### 30.1 Resolve tenant id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Basic {{tenantEmail}} {{tenantPass}}

> {%
client.global.set("tenant30_id", response.body.id);
%}

### 30.2 Landlord creates claim
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": {{tenant30_id}},
  "title": "Broken sofa and stained carpet",
  "description": "Tenant left visible damage; landlord requests damage assessment.",
  "claimedAmount": 250.00,
  "currency": "USD"
}

> {%
client.global.set("claim30_id", response.body.id);
%}

### 30.3 Read created claim (status SUBMITTED)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim30_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}

### 30.4 Admin starts intake
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim30_id}}/intake-start
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 30.5 Admin asks for additional info
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim30_id}}/intake-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestAdditionalInfo": true, "note": "Attach photos and serial numbers." }

### 30.6 Landlord provides additional info
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim30_id}}/additional-info
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Attached photos and the sofa serial number; carpet visible in room overview." }

### 30.7 Admin records assessment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim30_id}}/assessment
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "penaltyGrounds": true, "assessmentAmount": 175.00, "assessmentNotes": "Damage confirmed; reduced to fair value." }

### 30.8 Tenant disagrees
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim30_id}}/tenant-response
Authorization: Basic {{tenantEmail}} {{tenantPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "I disagree with the assessed amount." }

### 30.9 Support approves penalty
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim30_id}}/support-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applyPenalty": true,
  "penaltyAmount": 175.00,
  "penaltyCurrency": "USD",
  "simulateFailure": false,
  "resolutionNote": "Proceed with penalty application."
}

### 30.10 Poll claim (re-run until PENALTY_APPLIED — Outbox+Kafka are async)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim30_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 30.11 Claim status history
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim30_id}}/history
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 30.12 Penalty for this claim (penalty-service via proxy)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/penalties/claim/{{claim30_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
